1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,630
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,630 --> 00:00:04,980
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:05,970
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:07,350
I've been a millwright

5
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:08,480
for thirty years.

6
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:10,350
Crawling under machines

7
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:11,940
and kneeling on
concrete floors

8
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:12,640
to fix them.

9
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:13,900
I had my right knee

10
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,260
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:17,850
It has hurt every day
since.

12
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:19,010
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:20,800
I know what that felt
like,

14
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:21,720
and it went away.

15
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:22,860
This is different.

16
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:23,550
Tight.

17
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:24,290
Full.

18
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:25,240
Like a band around

19
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:26,860
the joint that never
loosens.

20
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:27,890
And for two years

21
00:00:27,890 --> 00:00:29,490
I've been told the same
thing.

22
00:00:29,490 --> 00:00:30,350
Give it time.

23
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:32,550
At six weeks it was
swelling,

24
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:34,060
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:35,070
At three months,

26
00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:36,110
give it six.

27
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:37,120
At six months,

28
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,780
some knees take a full
year.

29
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:39,490
At a year,

30
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:41,280
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

31
00:00:41,930 --> 00:00:43,180
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:44,580
We went down the list.

33
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:46,310
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:46,310 --> 00:00:47,470
Every session,

35
00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:49,030
every exercise at home.

36
00:00:49,530 --> 00:00:50,820
I got stronger.

37
00:00:50,820 --> 00:00:52,580
The tightness never moved.

38
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:54,050
The pain pills helped,

39
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:55,220
and that was the problem.

40
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:57,390
I'm already on enough
every morning,

41
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:58,530
and nobody could tell me

42
00:00:58,530 --> 00:01:00,040
when I'd get to stop.

43
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:01,410
Then a nerve block.

44
00:01:01,410 --> 00:01:03,320
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

45
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:04,860
And after that, a second

46
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:06,180
operation to go back

47
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:07,320
in and do it over.

48
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:08,740
I said no.

49
00:01:09,250 --> 00:01:11,600
Every morning I laced
up my work boots

50
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:12,660
and my knee felt like

51
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,150
a band was wrapped around
it,

52
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:16,410
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

53
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:18,010
Every morning I took
something

54
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:19,420
for it and went to work.

55
00:01:19,850 --> 00:01:21,260
Couldn't do the stairs,

56
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:22,430
couldn't stand at the
counter

57
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:23,860
long enough to finish
dinner,

58
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:25,790
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

59
00:01:25,790 --> 00:01:28,190
game without shifting
every two minutes.

60
00:01:28,510 --> 00:01:31,160
Couldn't kneel down
under a machine

61
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:32,640
to change a bearing

62
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:35,020
without grabbing something
to get back up.

63
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:36,830
The guys on my crew

64
00:01:36,830 --> 00:01:38,890
started taking the
low work for me.

65
00:01:39,170 --> 00:01:40,140
I started wondering

66
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:42,050
how many more years
I had left

67
00:01:42,050 --> 00:01:42,930
on that floor.

68
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:44,800
It woke me at night,

69
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,860
and it turned ordinary
things,

70
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:48,190
like getting in the car

71
00:01:48,530 --> 00:01:50,060
or up off the couch,

72
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:51,120
into a decision.

73
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:52,910
After a long and serious

74
00:01:52,910 --> 00:01:54,280
talk with my wife,

75
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,840
I went back in one more
time.

76
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:57,210
That was the fourth set

77
00:01:57,210 --> 00:01:58,690
of X-rays on this knee.

78
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:00,380
And like the three before
it,

79
00:02:00,690 --> 00:02:03,260
the answer was everything
looks great.

80
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:05,590
No loosening, no
infection,

81
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:06,520
nothing wrong.

82
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:07,690
Only this time there

83
00:02:07,690 --> 00:02:08,830
was no new number.

84
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:09,800
Nobody said

85
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:11,570
give it another six
months.

86
00:02:11,570 --> 00:02:13,210
There was nothing left to
give it.

87
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:14,440
I sat in the parking

88
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:15,550
lot for a while.

89
00:02:15,550 --> 00:02:17,000
Okay, I thought.

90
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,510
Then explain this.

91
00:02:18,510 --> 00:02:21,050
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

92
00:02:21,050 --> 00:02:22,770
I hit my breaking point.

93
00:02:22,770 --> 00:02:24,870
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

94
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:27,200
I had a shift
starting at six.

95
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,820
Everyone in the house was
asleep

96
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:30,700
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

97
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:31,800
with my leg up,

98
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:33,400
trying to find any angle
where

99
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,510
it didn't feel like
something

100
00:02:34,510 --> 00:02:35,590
was wrapped around my knee

101
00:02:35,590 --> 00:02:36,290
and tightening.

102
00:02:36,770 --> 00:02:39,060
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

103
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:41,390
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

104
00:02:41,810 --> 00:02:43,010
And I just thought,

105
00:02:43,010 --> 00:02:44,910
is this really my life
now?

106
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:46,470
I can't live like this.

107
00:02:46,470 --> 00:02:48,430
So I made myself a
promise.

108
00:02:48,430 --> 00:02:49,310
I wouldn't go a day

109
00:02:49,310 --> 00:02:50,720
without looking for an
answer.

110
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:52,210
And when I found one,

111
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:53,720
I'd share it with everyone

112
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:55,000
going through the same
thing.

113
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,450
So I got my laptop

114
00:02:56,450 --> 00:02:57,650
out and went looking.

115
00:02:58,030 --> 00:02:59,220
Not for a product.

116
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,220
For an explanation.

117
00:03:00,510 --> 00:03:01,990
Mayo Clinic forums,

118
00:03:02,270 --> 00:03:04,410
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

119
00:03:04,410 --> 00:03:07,360
doctor videos, medical
animations.

120
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,240
And that's when I found

121
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,840
a video from a physical
therapist

122
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:10,410
named Dr.

123
00:03:10,410 --> 00:03:13,000
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

124
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,920
had been through exactly
this.

125
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:17,320
But before I say anything
else,

126
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,660
I want to be straight with
you.

127
00:03:19,170 --> 00:03:21,300
You've already had
something work fast.

128
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:22,010
The ice.

129
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:24,070
The first week of a new
pill.

130
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:25,960
The good day after a
session.

131
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,260
Then it wore off.

132
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:30,130
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

133
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:32,220
Fast relief isn't relief.

134
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:33,690
It's a preview.

135
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,390
So I'm not going to tell

136
00:03:35,390 --> 00:03:36,620
you this works fast.

137
00:03:36,620 --> 00:03:37,250
It doesn't.

138
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:39,390
But if you're willing to
be patient,

139
00:03:39,390 --> 00:03:40,150
and to look at what's

140
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:41,930
going on around your new
knee

141
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:43,360
instead of inside it,
there

142
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:45,270
is a real reason it still
hurts.

143
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:47,250
And something you can do
about it.

144
00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:48,680
Let me explain what he
said,

145
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,790
because this is what
changed

146
00:03:50,790 --> 00:03:52,050
everything for me.

147
00:03:52,050 --> 00:03:54,050
He started with the
basics.

148
00:03:54,050 --> 00:03:55,660
A knee replacement takes
out

149
00:03:55,660 --> 00:03:57,800
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

150
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,260
in metal and plastic.

151
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:00,950
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

152
00:04:00,950 --> 00:04:02,650
you had before the
operation.

153
00:04:02,650 --> 00:04:04,250
That part I already knew.

154
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:05,790
But then he explained
something

155
00:04:05,790 --> 00:04:07,390
nobody had ever told me.

156
00:04:07,390 --> 00:04:08,200
He said,

157
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:09,580
think about a swollen foot

158
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:10,890
inside a shoe.

159
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:12,400
The shoe didn't shrink.

160
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,520
Your foot is taking up
more room,

161
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,770
so everything feels
cramped

162
00:04:16,770 --> 00:04:18,500
and tight and squeezed.

163
00:04:18,990 --> 00:04:20,100
Your new knee sits

164
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:21,630
in a limited space with
living

165
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:23,320
tissue packed all around
it.

166
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,570
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

167
00:04:25,570 --> 00:04:27,250
had to work through that
tissue.

168
00:04:27,620 --> 00:04:29,920
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

169
00:04:30,370 --> 00:04:32,160
At first that's normal.

170
00:04:32,490 --> 00:04:34,170
But in some people that
swelling can

171
00:04:34,170 --> 00:04:37,090
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

172
00:04:37,090 --> 00:04:38,830
And swollen tissue takes
up more

173
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:40,730
room than calm tissue
does.

174
00:04:40,730 --> 00:04:41,820
So when you bend,

175
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:43,900
that tissue gets
compressed.

176
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:44,820
When you straighten,

177
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:46,110
it gets pulled tight.

178
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:47,270
That's the band.

179
00:04:47,660 --> 00:04:49,750
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

180
00:04:50,130 --> 00:04:50,950
And you start being

181
00:04:50,950 --> 00:04:52,050
the one who says,

182
00:04:52,050 --> 00:04:52,800
you go ahead.

183
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:53,640
I'll stay here.

184
00:04:53,950 --> 00:04:55,840
And that's exactly why so
much

185
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:57,960
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

186
00:04:58,270 --> 00:05:00,390
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

187
00:05:00,390 --> 00:05:01,470
around the knee.

188
00:05:01,470 --> 00:05:02,680
Worth doing,

189
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:03,470
and I'd done it.

190
00:05:04,190 --> 00:05:05,630
It does nothing about
tissue

191
00:05:05,630 --> 00:05:06,790
taking up room.

192
00:05:06,790 --> 00:05:08,020
A nerve block quiets

193
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:09,870
the nerve carrying the
signal.

194
00:05:09,870 --> 00:05:11,540
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

195
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:13,220
But when that irritated
tissue

196
00:05:13,220 --> 00:05:14,710
finally calms down,

197
00:05:14,710 --> 00:05:16,050
it holds less fluid,

198
00:05:16,050 --> 00:05:17,430
and it takes up less room.

199
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:18,920
Less room taken up means

200
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,690
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

201
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:22,470
That's what takes the
pressure off.

202
00:05:22,470 --> 00:05:24,080
After two years of this,

203
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:25,420
it finally made sense.

204
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:27,810
The problem was never the
new knee.

205
00:05:27,810 --> 00:05:29,620
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

206
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:31,120
He calls it the squeeze.

207
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:33,210
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

208
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,850
I'd bought knee pads,
knee sleeves,

209
00:05:35,850 --> 00:05:38,030
compression braces,
creams,

210
00:05:38,030 --> 00:05:39,630
half of Amazon really,

211
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:40,960
and all any of it gave me

212
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:42,250
was an hour.

213
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:43,530
I even looked at going

214
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:45,460
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

215
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:47,620
But at $200 a session

216
00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:49,380
with nothing covered by
insurance,

217
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:50,800
that was a quick no.

218
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:52,210
Then one night I went

219
00:05:52,210 --> 00:05:53,430
back to that knee
replacement

220
00:05:53,430 --> 00:05:54,780
group and actually read
it.

221
00:05:55,170 --> 00:05:56,590
Thousands of people,

222
00:05:56,590 --> 00:05:58,100
years out from surgery,

223
00:05:58,100 --> 00:05:59,920
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

224
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:01,010
nobody could explain.

225
00:06:01,390 --> 00:06:02,860
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

226
00:06:02,860 --> 00:06:04,920
the same thing kept coming
up.

227
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,360
This one device,

228
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:08,100
and people saying it was
the first

229
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:09,870
thing that made a
difference.

230
00:06:10,250 --> 00:06:12,250
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

231
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:13,930
alright, here it comes,

232
00:06:13,930 --> 00:06:15,360
he's selling me something,

233
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:17,310
let me shut that down
right now.

234
00:06:17,310 --> 00:06:18,910
I'm only here because I
made myself

235
00:06:18,910 --> 00:06:20,770
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

236
00:06:20,770 --> 00:06:21,920
that if I ever found

237
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:23,060
something that helped,

238
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:23,990
I'd say so.

239
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:25,980
It's called the KenRelief
Red

240
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:27,270
Light Therapy Wrap.

241
00:06:27,270 --> 00:06:28,780
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

242
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:30,250
It looked like the cheap

243
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:31,750
knee sleeves off Amazon

244
00:06:31,750 --> 00:06:33,150
that did nothing for me.

245
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:35,340
But I went to their
website anyway,

246
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:36,220
just to see what all

247
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:37,470
the fuss was about.

248
00:06:37,470 --> 00:06:39,140
It's the same red light
therapy

249
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:42,110
clinics charge $200 a
session

250
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:44,230
for, off machines that
cost

251
00:06:44,230 --> 00:06:45,810
fifty thousand dollars,

252
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:46,850
in a wrap you plug

253
00:06:46,850 --> 00:06:47,930
into the wall at home.

254
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:50,190
Two hundred and forty
lights.

255
00:06:50,530 --> 00:06:53,280
Red at 660 nanometers

256
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:56,070
and near-infrared at 850,

257
00:06:56,070 --> 00:06:58,530
run together for the
strongest effect.

258
00:06:58,530 --> 00:06:59,970
Four strength levels.

259
00:06:59,970 --> 00:07:01,810
A five to thirty minute
timer.

260
00:07:02,250 --> 00:07:03,830
Then I saw the guarantee.

261
00:07:03,830 --> 00:07:05,070
Ninety days.

262
00:07:05,070 --> 00:07:06,770
Results or your money
back,

263
00:07:06,770 --> 00:07:09,300
no questions, no store
credit,

264
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:11,020
and you don't even send it
back.

265
00:07:11,430 --> 00:07:13,730
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

266
00:07:13,730 --> 00:07:15,450
days to change my mind.

267
00:07:15,450 --> 00:07:16,920
There wasn't much to lose,

268
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:17,960
so I ordered it.

269
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:19,700
Two of them, actually.

270
00:07:19,700 --> 00:07:21,570
Only the right knee was
replaced,

271
00:07:21,570 --> 00:07:23,380
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

272
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:25,040
and I'd done it for two
years.

273
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:27,740
The left one was carrying
the difference.

274
00:07:28,170 --> 00:07:29,170
When it came,

275
00:07:29,170 --> 00:07:31,000
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

276
00:07:31,410 --> 00:07:32,770
because I'd been let down
too

277
00:07:32,770 --> 00:07:34,160
many times to get excited.

278
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:36,070
What I felt was warmth.

279
00:07:36,070 --> 00:07:37,940
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

280
00:07:37,940 --> 00:07:39,530
More like it was coming
from inside

281
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:41,100
the knee and spreading
around it.

282
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:41,930
And that was it.

283
00:07:42,250 --> 00:07:43,670
That was the whole
experience.

284
00:07:44,150 --> 00:07:45,450
When I took it off,

285
00:07:45,450 --> 00:07:46,310
I'll be honest,

286
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:48,710
nothing dramatic had
happened.

287
00:07:49,090 --> 00:07:51,100
And after what that video
said,

288
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:52,990
that's exactly what I
expected.

289
00:07:53,350 --> 00:07:54,310
What was different

290
00:07:54,610 --> 00:07:55,510
was that for the first

291
00:07:55,510 --> 00:07:56,800
time in two years

292
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,440
I'd done something for my
knee

293
00:07:58,440 --> 00:07:59,290
instead of to it.

294
00:07:59,930 --> 00:08:00,750
Twenty minutes,

295
00:08:00,750 --> 00:08:02,780
in my own chair,
after work.

296
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:04,250
No drive, no copay.

297
00:08:04,250 --> 00:08:05,870
They say twenty minutes.

298
00:08:06,180 --> 00:08:07,150
I did thirty,

299
00:08:07,510 --> 00:08:08,540
twice a day,

300
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:10,490
lowest setting that first
week.

301
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:11,890
I put it on the calendar.

302
00:08:11,890 --> 00:08:12,860
The first week,

303
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:13,700
I couldn't have told

304
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:15,290
you if anything was
happening.

305
00:08:15,290 --> 00:08:16,190
I tried not to get

306
00:08:16,190 --> 00:08:17,160
my hopes up.

307
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,740
I'd had things help for a
week

308
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:19,920
and then stop.

309
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:21,360
But somewhere in the
second week

310
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:22,610
I noticed I'd come down

311
00:08:22,610 --> 00:08:24,500
the stairs without holding
the rail.

312
00:08:24,910 --> 00:08:26,510
I hadn't decided to.

313
00:08:26,510 --> 00:08:27,530
I just did it,

314
00:08:27,530 --> 00:08:29,650
then stopped halfway down

315
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:30,910
because I realized.

316
00:08:31,330 --> 00:08:32,640
By the end of the fourth
week

317
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:33,850
I'd slept through the
night

318
00:08:33,850 --> 00:08:35,130
four times running.

319
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,480
I stood at the counter

320
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,580
and finished making dinner

321
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:39,020
without looking for the
stool.

322
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,060
None of that is dramatic.

323
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:41,950
All of it was gone

324
00:08:41,950 --> 00:08:43,180
for two years.

325
00:08:43,180 --> 00:08:44,780
A few weeks later my wife
asked

326
00:08:44,780 --> 00:08:45,790
if I wanted to walk

327
00:08:45,790 --> 00:08:47,700
the long way around the
block.

328
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:48,770
And for the first time

329
00:08:48,770 --> 00:08:49,870
in two years,

330
00:08:49,870 --> 00:08:50,910
I said yes.

331
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:53,230
I wanted to understand
why,

332
00:08:53,230 --> 00:08:54,670
so I read the whole thing.

333
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,850
It comes down to four
steps.

334
00:08:56,850 --> 00:08:57,340
One.

335
00:08:57,750 --> 00:08:59,600
The tissue around a new
knee can

336
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:03,010
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

337
00:09:03,010 --> 00:09:03,720
Two.

338
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:06,010
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

339
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:07,290
so it takes up more

340
00:09:07,290 --> 00:09:08,440
room than it should.

341
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:09,260
Three.

342
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:10,930
There's only so much room
in there.

343
00:09:10,930 --> 00:09:12,720
Bending compresses it.

344
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,170
Straightening pulls it
tight.

345
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:15,820
That's the squeeze.

346
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:16,400
Four.

347
00:09:16,830 --> 00:09:18,990
Red and near-infrared
light have been

348
00:09:18,990 --> 00:09:21,180
studied for calming that
inflammation,

349
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:22,460
so the swelling and the
pressure

350
00:09:22,460 --> 00:09:23,860
can come down with it.

351
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:25,390
In a randomized trial,

352
00:09:25,390 --> 00:09:27,140
patients given light
therapy after

353
00:09:27,140 --> 00:09:28,010
a knee replacement

354
00:09:28,010 --> 00:09:29,200
had less pain,

355
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:29,970
less swelling

356
00:09:29,970 --> 00:09:31,300
and better early movement
than

357
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:32,190
those who weren't.

358
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:35,390
A 2025 review said the
same,

359
00:09:35,390 --> 00:09:36,530
and was clear the evidence

360
00:09:36,530 --> 00:09:37,490
is still limited.

361
00:09:37,870 --> 00:09:39,520
I probably sound like a
broken record

362
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,800
to the guys on my crew.

363
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:43,340
But after two years of
doing everything

364
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:45,050
I was told and getting
nowhere,

365
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,640
you have no idea what it's

366
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:48,260
like to sleep through the
night,

367
00:09:48,260 --> 00:09:49,720
say yes to the walk,

368
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:51,170
and get my life back.

369
00:09:51,170 --> 00:09:52,490
So take it from me.

370
00:09:52,490 --> 00:09:53,910
Don't spend another year
waiting

371
00:09:53,910 --> 00:09:54,910
for it to settle.

372
00:09:54,910 --> 00:09:56,710
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

373
00:09:56,710 --> 00:09:58,170
More than ten thousand
people

374
00:09:58,170 --> 00:09:59,180
with pain after a knee

375
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:01,080
replacement have already
tried this.

376
00:10:01,390 --> 00:10:02,740
Some had it worse than I
did.

377
00:10:03,090 --> 00:10:04,230
You can get the KenRelief

378
00:10:04,230 --> 00:10:05,680
wrap from their website,

379
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:06,750
with a discount link

380
00:10:06,750 --> 00:10:08,160
and ninety days to try it.

381
00:10:08,610 --> 00:10:10,390
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

382
00:10:10,390 --> 00:10:11,650
you get your money back

383
00:10:11,650 --> 00:10:12,970
and you keep the wrap.

384
00:10:12,970 --> 00:10:14,370
They only release so many

385
00:10:14,370 --> 00:10:15,460
at that price.

386
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:16,590
If it's still there,

387
00:10:16,590 --> 00:10:17,170
get one,

388
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:18,980
and stop the squeeze.

